---
description: Shared React Native and Expo mobile engineering baseline
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the Mobile Engineering Playbook as the shared baseline:

https://github.com/sergii/mobile-engineering-playbook

Always read this product repository's local instructions and task-relevant domain documentation first.

Load shared guidance only when relevant:

- architecture/startup/unfamiliar mobile decision → `MOBILE_ENGINEERING_PLAYBOOK.md`
- adding/adopting a dependency → `guides/decision-ladder.md`
- suspicious generated/overbuilt code → `guides/agent-failure-modes.md`
- native config, auth/security boundaries, storage, safe areas, keyboard, OTA/native compatibility, lifecycle-sensitive behavior, `ios/` or `android/` → `guides/platform-native-rules.md`
- finishing a meaningful slice → `guides/vertical-slice-checklist.md`
- explicitly selected archetype → read it only for relevant tasks

Product-specific rules override generic examples. Do not silently select an archetype and do not load every shared guide for every task.

Default behavior:

- build thin vertical slices before broad infrastructure;
- prefer React Native and Expo primitives;
- start with `StyleSheet` and strict TypeScript;
- add dependencies only when they solve demonstrated problems;
- determine CNG/native-project ownership before editing generated native files;
- keep auth identity, credential storage, route protection, server authorization, profile data, and app state separate;
- never treat client route protection as backend authorization;
- prefer declarative Expo Router route protection;
- verify meaningful UI/native behavior in the running mobile runtime;
- verify interruption/restart behavior when the workflow depends on it.

Keep product-specific domain rules local to the product repository instead of duplicating the shared playbook here.
